WEBVTT

00:00:00.645 --> 00:00:01.550
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.794 --> 00:00:05.150
In this lesson, we file each nail shape, step by step.

00:00:05.659 --> 00:00:07.470
Keep in mind three things throughout:

00:00:07.578 --> 00:00:11.051
all ten nails the same length, the tip on the center line,

00:00:11.001 --> 00:00:13.470
and no filing deep into the side corners.

00:00:14.068 --> 00:00:14.849
Step one:

00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:16.289
agree with the client.

00:00:16.695 --> 00:00:20.013
Wash and sanitize your hands, and the hands of the client,

00:00:19.963 --> 00:00:23.169
then look closely at the nails and the skin around them.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.369
Ask which shape the client likes, and how long.

00:00:26.797 --> 00:00:28.811
Show the client pictures of the shapes,

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:31.329
and tell her honestly which shape suits her nails,

00:00:31.437 --> 00:00:32.609
as in the theory lesson.

00:00:33.205 --> 00:00:33.975
Step two:

00:00:34.209 --> 00:00:36.375
set the length first, then the shape.

00:00:36.781 --> 00:00:41.130
If the nails are much too long, trim them with nail clippers, a little at a time,

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:42.775
leaving a bit extra for filing.

00:00:43.245 --> 00:00:47.015
If a nail is only slightly long, file straight across to shorten it.

00:00:47.355 --> 00:00:50.215
Make every nail the same length before you start shaping.

00:00:50.557 --> 00:00:55.006
If a nail has broken short, the overall length follows the shortest nail,

00:00:54.956 --> 00:00:57.175
or that nail gets its own extension,

00:00:57.426 --> 00:00:59.735
as in the lesson on extensions on forms.

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:01.097
Step three:

00:01:01.506 --> 00:01:04.057
look at the nail from above, and from the tip.

00:01:04.474 --> 00:01:06.217
Find the center line of the nail.

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:09.004
Then find the stress points, on each side,

00:01:08.954 --> 00:01:11.417
where the nail starts to leave the skin bed.

00:01:11.923 --> 00:01:13.497
Every shape starts from there:

00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:16.747
the side walls run straight out from the stress points,

00:01:16.697 --> 00:01:18.617
and the tip sits on the center line.

00:01:19.242 --> 00:01:22.628
Hold the file lightly, slightly angled under the free edge.

00:01:23.032 --> 00:01:27.914
On natural nails, file in a single direction, from the side towards the center,

00:01:27.864 --> 00:01:29.748
and do not saw back and forth.

00:01:30.073 --> 00:01:32.228
Use a fine file for natural nails.

00:01:32.577 --> 00:01:34.548
Coarser files are only for enhancements.

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:38.329
Keep the finger of the client lying straight, not tilted.

00:01:38.815 --> 00:01:41.339
If the finger tilts, the file tilts with it,

00:01:41.289 --> 00:01:44.489
and the nail ends up lopsided without you even noticing.

00:01:45.068 --> 00:01:47.289
Keep your eyes on the center line of the nail.

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:52.009
And keep the same filing angle on both sides, so both sides come out equal.

00:01:52.607 --> 00:01:53.466
Step four:

00:01:53.637 --> 00:01:54.266
shaping.

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:56.186
First, the square shape.

00:01:56.452 --> 00:02:00.585
Hold the file at a right angle to the finger, and file straight across the tip.

00:02:00.848 --> 00:02:03.306
Then file the side walls straight and parallel.

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:07.930
Finally, glide lightly over the corners, just to take off the sharpness,

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:09.146
so they do not catch.

00:02:09.493 --> 00:02:12.026
Square looks best on short to medium nails.

00:02:12.272 --> 00:02:15.386
The longer the nail, the more easily square corners break.

00:02:15.974 --> 00:02:16.664
Squoval:

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:19.864
first do exactly the same as for square.

00:02:20.292 --> 00:02:25.127
Then round off both corners a little more, with a few short strokes on each corner,

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:25.704
in an arc.

00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:28.104
Both corners must be rounded equally.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:29.391
Round:

00:02:29.493 --> 00:02:30.511
for short nails.

00:02:30.839 --> 00:02:34.911
File from the side, following the curve of the fingertip, up to the center.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:37.791
Then do the other side exactly the same way.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:41.391
The tip is a single even curve, with no straight part.

00:02:41.822 --> 00:02:46.191
This shape suits male clients very well, and people who work a lot with their hands.

00:02:46.753 --> 00:02:47.396
Oval:

00:02:47.624 --> 00:02:49.236
the nail needs a bit more length.

00:02:49.556 --> 00:02:53.032
File both sides into an even curve, meeting at a rounded tip,

00:02:52.982 --> 00:02:54.436
right on the center line.

00:02:54.839 --> 00:02:59.236
Be careful not to file the sides in too deep, or the oval turns into an almond.

00:02:59.571 --> 00:03:00.436
A small trick:

00:03:00.785 --> 00:03:03.156
imagine the tip is the narrow end of an egg.

00:03:03.744 --> 00:03:04.273
Almond:

00:03:04.621 --> 00:03:07.472
keep the side walls straight from the stress points,

00:03:07.422 --> 00:03:10.433
then file diagonally from each side towards the middle,

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:13.233
tapering into a soft, rounded point.

00:03:13.662 --> 00:03:18.244
Finish one side, look again from above, and only then file the other side,

00:03:18.194 --> 00:03:19.713
so both sides are equal.

00:03:20.295 --> 00:03:24.501
On strong natural nails, a short to medium almond is the most beautiful,

00:03:24.451 --> 00:03:25.713
and the most durable.

00:03:26.349 --> 00:03:27.009
Coffin:

00:03:27.178 --> 00:03:31.089
file diagonally on both sides like an almond, but stop earlier.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.557
Then hold the file at a right angle, and file straight across the tip,

00:03:35.507 --> 00:03:37.009
leaving a small flat end.

00:03:37.437 --> 00:03:41.649
Both tapered sides must be the same length, and the flat end sits in the middle.

00:03:42.078 --> 00:03:45.409
This shape needs length, so it is usually done on enhancements.

00:03:45.918 --> 00:03:46.607
Stiletto:

00:03:46.779 --> 00:03:51.887
file both sides diagonally, even more steeply, to a sharp point right in the center.

00:03:52.218 --> 00:03:56.047
This shape is only for enhancements, or very strong natural nails.

00:03:56.308 --> 00:04:00.687
On enhancements, use a coarser file, and go gently near the natural nail.

00:04:01.283 --> 00:04:03.093
A trick many technicians use:

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:07.733
do the same step on all five fingers, then move on to the next step.

00:04:08.079 --> 00:04:13.645
For example, file the left side of all five nails, then the right side of all five,

00:04:13.595 --> 00:04:15.573
and only then shape the tips.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:20.773
That way, your hand keeps the same filing angle, and the nails come out more even.

00:04:21.422 --> 00:04:22.307
Step five:

00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:23.587
check each nail.

00:04:23.914 --> 00:04:24.707
From above:

00:04:25.056 --> 00:04:27.587
is the tip in the middle, are both sides equal?

00:04:28.053 --> 00:04:30.147
Turn the finger, and look from the tip:

00:04:30.416 --> 00:04:31.587
are the sides balanced?

00:04:32.084 --> 00:04:36.387
Then put both hands side by side, and compare all ten nails.

00:04:36.724 --> 00:04:40.227
Wherever something is off, fix it now, with a few light strokes.

00:04:40.496 --> 00:04:42.307
And look from the side of the client too:

00:04:42.417 --> 00:04:46.947
turn her hand around, and look at it exactly the way she will look at her own hands.

00:04:47.632 --> 00:04:48.567
Step six:

00:04:48.739 --> 00:04:49.367
finishing.

00:04:49.867 --> 00:04:53.256
Glide a fine buffer very lightly under the edge of the tip,

00:04:53.206 --> 00:04:54.727
to remove any tiny fibers.

00:04:55.065 --> 00:04:57.207
Brush off the dust with a soft brush.

00:04:57.552 --> 00:05:00.327
Dust from enhancements is extracted, not blown.

00:05:00.838 --> 00:05:05.527
Then put a drop of cuticle oil on the skin around the nails, and massage gently.

00:05:06.143 --> 00:05:08.106
Before the client leaves, tell her:

00:05:08.587 --> 00:05:12.026
if a nail chips or catches, do not bite it or tear it.

00:05:12.531 --> 00:05:17.466
Use a fine file, filing lightly in a single direction, or come back to the salon.

00:05:17.972 --> 00:05:22.449
And note the shape and length the client chose in her client record, so next time,

00:05:22.399 --> 00:05:24.986
whoever does her nails can do exactly the same.

00:05:25.581 --> 00:05:27.787
Beautiful shaping does not need speed.

00:05:28.121 --> 00:05:32.107
It needs consistency, balance, and a shape that suits the client.

00:05:32.608 --> 00:05:35.867
Practice each shape slowly, and your hands will get faster.

00:05:36.129 --> 00:05:38.747
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
